%N A402522 Triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of simple connected graphs on n unlabeled vertices with exactly k simplicial vertices.
%C A402522 A simplicial vertex is one whose neighbors induce a complete graph.
%C A402522 The set of simplicial vertices is also equal to the intersection of all hull sets in the graph (a hull set is a set of vertices whose convex hull is the entire graph).
%H A402522 Chı́nh. T Hoàng, Stefan Hougardy, Frédéric Maffray and N.V.R. Mahadev, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/S0166-218X(03)00275-0">On simplicial and co-simplicial vertices in graphs</a>, Discrete Applied Mathematics 138, (2004) 117-132.
%H A402522 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simplicial_vertex">Simplicial vertex</a>.
